    LLM: 'Game: Wall Street Poker. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Wall Street Poker is a Seven-Card Stud variant with buyable community cards. 2-7 players. 52-card deck. Deal 3 hole cards (2 down, 1 up). 4 community cards ('Wall Street') placed face-up with escalating costs (1-4 units). Players can buy a community card (goes to pot) or get a free card from deck. Named after aggressive financial bidding.",
    objective: 'Make the best high hand and/or the best low hand from your seven cards; after declaration, the high winner and the low winner split the pot.',
    gameplay: 'Wall Street: 4 community cards face-up costing 1/2/3/4 units. Each round: buy a community card (fee to pot, card replaced from deck) OR get free face-up card. Continue until 4 upcards each. Final card dealt face-down. Standard betting rounds. Best 5-card hand wins.',
